with the conversational AI

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.710
technology.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.470
This is, obviously, because
they have Google Homes.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.600
They use search on
their Android phone.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.600
90% of them are familiar
with those technologies,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.960
and 72% have used
voice assistant.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.550
That means that
consumers are getting

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.350
trained on those technology.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.120
They are getting
more comfortable

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.920
using their voice to do
something to ask of Google

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.930
or ask of any of
their application

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.970
on a day to day basis.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.010
There was a trend in the
past where we thought

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.360
chat would replace voice.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.350
It's not happening.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.590
Voice is growing
very fast, and CCAI

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.180
is there to answer that call.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.240
So what is CCAI?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.750
CCAI is really three
products inside Google.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.960
We have Dialogflow for
automating interactions

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.080
and self-service, we
have Agent Assist that

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.620
is used to help an agent
in a contact center

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.810
deliver a stellar
experience, and we

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.880
have a little newborn,
CCAI Insights,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.410
which is in alpha right now.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.150
Really helps you
understand all that

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.740
is happening in your contact
center, the code writers,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.050
et cetera.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.820
So before we dive
into those products,

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.970
