00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.160
ANTONY PASSEMARD: So
what you've seen here

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.240
is an example experience
of using first Dialogflow

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.340
for that self-service
experience,

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.150
getting context, helping the
customer as much as possible,

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:16.579
doing back end calls, getting
the information to them

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:18.610
in order to solve a problem.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.839
But when the call needs to
be escalated to an agent,

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:25.790
Dialogflow transitions
very smoothly to the agent,

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.980
gives all the
conversation context,

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.230
anything that happened
so the customer does not

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.500
have to repeat again, something
very frustrating for customer.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.797
Repeat information, [INAUDIBLE]
themself to whatever.

00:04:36.797 --> 00:04:39.380
This is all taken care of by the
transition between Dialogflow

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.710
and Agent Assist.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.890
The conversation's
picked up right away.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.110
The agent is assisted
in real time.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.610
No need for the agent
to search on their own.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.070
They'll get
information proactively

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.740
thanks to Agent Assist,
and then all the insights

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:57.200
in the back end are helpful for
coach, QAs, product managers,

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.600
any person in relation
to the activities that

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.500
are going on in the contact
center will use that.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.120
This experience is
possible because we have

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.610
a fully integrated product.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.130
It's an end to end solution
for a contact center

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.220
starting with advanced
conversational AI

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:16.220
technology at the core, the text
to speech, the speech to text,

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.970
and the NLU who are powering
the virtual agent for voice

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.930
and chat as well as the human
agent with real time prompts

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.240
Agent Assist, and even
Dialogflow bots that

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:27.870
can help the human agent.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:32.510
All of that data being created,
all of those interactions,

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:35.750
are being fed into
Insights to have

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:40.940
a holistic view of all channels
across the contact center

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.620
and really understand
what is going on.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.430
When we're looking at the value
created by Contact Center AI,

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.600
we see two main links.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.790
The first one is
the human agent.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.570
How do we help a human agent
with Contact Center AI?

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.570
Well, by bringing
those suggestions

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.620
to the human agent
at the right time

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.790
with context
understanding of what's

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:08.350
going on in the conversation,
the human agent will be faster,

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.540
will have more
accurate responses,

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.400
will provide better information.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.400
Better data will be
relevant and look very good,

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.920
like a powerful agent.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.670
Look like they know
what they're doing.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.980
And that's very important
because the human agent

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.720
will feel empowered.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.790
They'll feel like a super agent.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:27.500
And that's a better
experience for the agent,

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.200
which means a better experience
for your customers eventually.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.058
It will also reduce churn.

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.850
Churn is a big problem
in a contact center,

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.230
as you probably know.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.920
Between six months to 12 months
for a full contact center

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.410
refresh of agents,
that's not good.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.250
Training costs are hard.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:46.540
The skill level of
agents is not perfect.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:51.010
With Agent Assist, we can
really help solve that problem

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:54.580
and make sure that human agents
can do a good job right away,

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.200
feel good about their
job, and provide

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.320
the best experience
for your consumer

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.720
or the people calling
in your contact center.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.020
The second links are the
customers, the consumers,

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.630
the constituents sometimes.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:10.180
They get self-service
channel 24/7

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.627
through conversational
chat bots and agents.

00:07:12.627 --> 00:07:13.210
This is great.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:16.570
They can really have their
problem answered whenever

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:18.470
they're available for it.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.640
They have shorter
call time with agents.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.248
The agent knows everything
after transitioning from an IVR

00:07:24.248 --> 00:07:24.790
to the agent.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.740
The agent has all
the information.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.330
They get the information faster.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.200
The calls are shorter.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.600
The first call resolution
rate increases,

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:35.780
and the brand loyalty as a
consequence and the trust

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.680
to your brand and
to your institution,

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.660
your organization
are greatly improved.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.090
So those two core
sets of value--

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.490
human agent and
customer-- are really

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:48.220
what CCAI helps to
deliver, and we really

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.810
understand the
challenges that are

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:52.540
common across contact center.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:54.670
You're seeing ramping
operational costs.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:57.160
You're seeing long
average handle time.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.900
You're not having enough agent.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:02.920
Especially in this time of a
pandemic where the demand is

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.590
exploding contact
center cannot follow.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.670
They have to turn to technology.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.020
They're facing high
turnover, costly training,

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.350
lack of visibility
using sampling to know

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.302
what's going on in
the contact center.

00:08:15.302 --> 00:08:17.260
With Contact Center
Insights we can solve that.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.230
There's seasonality
issues they need to solve.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:22.480
Really, Contact
Center AI is there

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.450
to solve all those problems
across your contact center

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.070
challenges.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.140
A great example that
happened actually

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.830
at the beginning of the pandemic
with the state of Illinois.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.909
Unfortunately, many
people have lost their job

00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:37.010
during this pandemic.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:38.730
This is very bad.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.559
And they had to file
claims for unemployment.

00:08:41.559 --> 00:08:43.610
And in the state of
Illinois, they've

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:48.680
seen 3.2 million inquiries
in the first two weeks.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.610
This is massive.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.740
This is something they've
never seen before.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.380
How could they handle this?

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:57.320
They quickly deployed
Contact Center AI

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.320
with an agent to help them
answer unemployment claims.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.060
They've handled more than
2.6 million voice and chat

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.200
interaction through
the Virtual Agent,

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.830
and have been able to
answer 99.9% of clean claims

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.670
in a timely manner.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.430
The results is astounding.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.350
Very quickly set
up using partners

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:21.200
like Quantifphi, and
Cisco, and Presidio,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.330
they've been able to
set that up quickly

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.760
and serve their
constituent in the state.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.830
That was a great
success story for them,

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:32.480
for us in a very difficult time.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:35.530
So let's look at the
key CCAI offerings.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.530
Let's focus first on Dialogflow.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.600
We mentioned Dialogflow
with a self-service tool

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:45.880
to build bots and make sure
that customers can interact.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.300
Dialogflow has been in
market for a long time.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.600
It's been about
three, four years now.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.540
The transition was taken
more than two years ago

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:58.080
to focus on enterprise use cases
and contact center use cases.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.260
Thanks to that,
it's been deployed

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.710
in customers like Discovery, a
financial services firm; Marks

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:08.150
and Spencer in retail;
Verizon for telco;

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:11.480
we have digital
native companies;

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.210
other financial services,
fortune 10 retailer

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.950
